    Assertion:a-call-is-answered,sentence:a call is answered by the body that holds the thing — its view lands on the asking Remote and volatile keys stay off the snap
    Assertion:a-refused-call-names,sentence:a refused call names its why on the Remote and leaves the thing as it was — the next answer clears it
    Assertion:both-envelopes-of-a,sentence:both envelopes of a call are dropped once it is answered — and its optimistic wish retires with them
  step=4,dige:a20a91c482ab2728
    Assertion:a-call-from-outside,sentence:a call from outside my crew lands nothing — the road ignores it and the thing is untouched
    Assertion:a-call-nobody-answers,sentence:a call nobody answers expires on its own — the Remote says nobody answered and the row goes
    Assertion:the-same-verb-runs,sentence:the same verb runs locally on the real thing and remotely through a Remote — one kind serves both
    Assertion:list-names-every-target,sentence:list names every target of a kind on the backend
    Assertion:a-call-whose-doer,sentence:a call whose doer throws stays serving and is logged — never silently answered
